ner with accusative of congnate meaning with verb, בַּז Num 31:32 ; Isa 10:6 (|| שָׁלָל שָׁלַל , as often) 33:23 ; Ezek 29:19 ; 38:12-13 , בִּזָּה 2Chr 25:13 ; שָׁלָל Deut 3:7 ; 20:14 (both followed by לְ with reflexive suffix) 2Chr 20:25 (twice in verse); 28:8 ; Est 3:13 ; 8:11 ; בהמה & שׁלל Josh 8:2 , 27 ; 11:14 (all followed by לְ with reflexive suffix); object person carried off (compare בַּז ) Gen 34:29 ( ᵑ0 , but compare Ol); plunder, despoil , with accusative of person robbed Isa 10:2 ; 11:14 ; 17:14 ( שׁסה ) 42:22 (|| id. ) Zeph 2:9 ; Jer 30:16 ; Ezek 39:10 (twice in verse); with בָּהֶם (person) 1Sam 14:36 ; with accusative of place plundered Gen 34:27 ; 2Kin 7:16 ; 2Chr 14:13 ; absolute Num 31:53 ; Isa 42:24 . Niph`al Perfect וְנָבֹ֫זוּ consecutive Amos 3:11 ; Imperfect 2masculine singular תִּבּוֺז Isa 24:3 ; Infinitive absolute הִבּוֺז 24:3 — be spoiled, plundered , subject ארמנות Amos 3:11 ; הארץ Isa 24:3 ; תִּבּוֺז הִבּוֺז (|| תִּבּוֺק הִבּוֺק ). Pu`al Perfect וּבֻזָּ֑זוּ consecutive Jer 50:37 — be taken as spoil , subject אוצרת .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 14 36","keyReferences":["1Sam 14 36","2Chr 14 13","2Chr 20 25","2Chr 20 25","2Chr 25 13","2Chr 28 8","2Kgs 7 16","Amos 3 11"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":43,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 14 36","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":36,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְֽ/נָבֹ֥זָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqh1cp"},{"reference":"2Chr 14 13","book":"2Chr","chapter":14,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יָּבֹ֨זּוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"2Chr 20 25","book":"2Chr","chapter":20,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ/בֹ֣ז","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vqc"},{"reference":"2Chr 20 25","book":"2Chr","chapter":20,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֹּזְזִ֥ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmpa"},{"r